    14	/**
    15	 * Tier → seat-eligible-model priority. Hand-maintained per
    16	 * docs/procedures/MODEL-CARD.md's priority-ordered tier table — deliberately
    17	 * NOT parsed from the markdown (the card is prose/rationale, this is the
    18	 * compiled fact). Keep the two in sync by hand when the card changes.
    19	 *
    20	 * Only models that can hold a pi-native AgentHost seat are listed. The card's
    21	 * Sol (codex-exec cross-model pass) and Terra/Luna (codex bulk/mechanical)
    22	 * are explicitly out — the card states they "cannot hold a seat" / "cannot
    23	 * hold a pi session".
    24	 *
    25	 * Each tier is PRIORITY-ORDERED and resolution takes the first candidate whose
    26	 * `envVar` is present in the host process, so the fallback is a funding
    27	 * fallback: a host with no Anthropic key still seats every tier on the
    28	 * provider it can actually pay for. Before gh-1187 S0 this map was
    29	 * Anthropic-only, which meant a Google-funded instance composed every seat
    30	 * with NO resolved model and silently fell through to the host default — the
    31	 * tier ladder in policy.yaml was decorative there (#1195).
    32	 */
