    92	  /**
    93	   * Root of the workspace the `user` filesystem serves, or `null` when the
    94	   * host resolves a DIFFERENT root per request (core, the CLI hub) and so has
    95	   * no single one at fleet-composition time.
    96	   *
    97	   * Required, because published `instructionFiles` are addressed relative to
    98	   * it and only the caller knows it. It is NOT derivable from the discovered
    99	   * package roots: a fleet can be composed from packages that live outside
   100	   * the workspace root, and guessing produced well-formed paths that
   101	   * resolved to nothing.
   102	   *
   103	   * `null` is not a soft option — it makes the host structurally unable to
   104	   * publish a ref it cannot guarantee, which is the honest answer for
   105	   * per-workspace roots.
   106	   */
